Replacing those file versions updates their existing article references. Review [[Hollow Halls]] and all six hall articles after upload.

=== Existing world tiles ===

The wiki JPEG filenames are <code>0_0.jpg</code> through <code>7_7.jpg</code>. Use the corresponding files in <code>world/wiki/</code>, following the manifest's exact filename and position. Reusing these names preserves the existing background references.

A differently named PNG does not replace an existing JPEG tile. Changing filenames, world bounds or the background definition requires a separate deliberate wiki change; protected definitions may require an administrator.

The tested 20,480 × 20,480 world master is 188,561,736 bytes and exceeds the configured 15 MiB limit. Keep it as a local lossless master and use the tile output for the interactive map. An oversized master is marked ineligible. The tool does not silently resize or reduce quality to fit the limit. If any tile is ineligible, review that delivery before uploading it.

== Report a problem ==

Retain <code>failure.txt</code>, <code>run.json</code>, input verification and the relevant parser or native-helper log. Include the generator version, client build, selected options and failing stage in the report.

Do not attach game archives, extracted game resources or private account files. A supported unmodified client and a fresh output folder are the baseline for reproducing a failure.
